00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.460
Welcome to Sim. My name is Will, and I'll
be your instructor throughout Sim Academy.

00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:08.880
In this series, we'll go over the
fundamentals of how Sim works and get you

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:13.520
comfortable with the building blocks. The
platform has so much to offer that it's

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:17.580
easy to get overwhelmed, but once you
master the basics, you'll be able to build

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:22.800
your own agents and AI systems beyond
basic automations and chatbots. I'm

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:24.120
excited. Let's get started.

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:30.360
Sim is a workspace where everything you
build lives, your data, your workflows,

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:33.660
all in one place, and your whole team can
work in it together.

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:40.380
Everything in a workspace is one of two
kinds. Resources hold what your system

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:44.800
knows, your knowledge bases, tables, and
files. Workflows do the work, the agents

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:49.940
that turn that data into action.
Everything you build in Sim is made from a

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:53.640
few main object types. These are the seven
you'll work with. Let's walk through them

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:55.720
quickly and see what each one is for.

00:00:57.580 --> 00:01:02.340
The first is the workflow, an executable
process. Each block is one step. This one

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:07.340
classifies a customer message and drafts a
reply. Your system's steps live here.

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:13.440
Tables hold your structured data, rows,
and columns of statuses, scores, and

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:19.540
outputs. Anything you want to inspect or
process repeatedly belongs in a table. A

00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:24.600
knowledge base is searchable memory over
your documents. You ask it a question, and

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:30.780
it finds the most relevant material. Here,
the quarterly report. Files are the

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:35.080
documents and artifacts your workspace
holds onto. Some you upload, like this

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:39.800
report, and workflows can generate new
ones, like this summary. Integrations

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:43.980
connect your workflows and agents to the
outside world. Services like Gmail,

00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:49.020
Notion, and Airtable. A workflow can read
from these integrations and act through

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:53.880
them. Every time something runs, Sim
records what happened. That record is a

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:59.440
log. It lists each step that ran with its
timing and the output it produced. A

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:04.460
deployment makes a workflow usable outside
the editor. Publish it as a tool, and

00:02:04.460 --> 00:02:09.180
other AI systems, like Cursor or Claude
Code, can call your workflow on demand

00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:14.200
over MCP. And it all comes together in the
workflow. Let's open one up.
